<section class="section" id="architecture">
  <div class="section__inner">
    <p class="section__eyebrow">Architektur</p>
    <h2 class="section__title">Control Plane und Dataplane auf dem Host</h2>
    <p class="section__lead">
      Startreihenfolge <code>vz-net</code> → <code>vz-edge</code> → <code>vz-supervisor</code>.
      Pro VM läuft ein Helper, der die VirtualMachine besitzt.
    </p>
    <div class="pipeline">
      <div class="pipeline__step">
        <p class="pipeline__name">vz-net</p>
        <p class="pipeline__desc">vmnet-Refs, Host-Bridges und Attachment-Handles.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline__step">
        <p class="pipeline__name">vz-edge</p>
        <p class="pipeline__desc">DNS, Ports, Ingress, OIDC und Host-Dataplane.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline__step">
        <p class="pipeline__name">vz-supervisor</p>
        <p class="pipeline__desc">Desired State, SQLite, Apply-Pipeline und REST-API.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline__step">
        <p class="pipeline__name">vz-helper</p>
        <p class="pipeline__desc">Eine Instanz pro VM — besitzt VZVirtualMachine.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
